From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Subject: [PATCH] kk: reject unsupported buffer-backed images before Metal

STEAMAC-3F/6Y (appid 1174180, Apple M3): binding an image aborts in
mtl_new_texture_with_descriptor_linear with "Linear texture: cannot be
mipmapped, mipmapLevelCount (7) disallowed". The format query already
advertises maxMipLevels=1, maxArrayLayers=1 and sampleCounts=1 for LINEAR;
it is not an over-advertised mip limit. kk_image_init nevertheless accepts
seven levels, kk_image_layout_calc_linear only allocates level zero, and
binding forwards all seven levels to Metal's buffer texture constructor.

The layout is linear exactly when VkImageTiling is not OPTIMAL. Host
pointer import does not turn an optimal image into a linear one: 0016
creates a private heap for that case. Keep that path unrestricted. The
event lacks original VkImageCreateInfo arguments, so it cannot distinguish
LINEAR from the non-optimal DRM modifier path, which has the same limits.

Reject mipmapped, multi-layer, 3D and multisample non-optimal images with
VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED in image initialization, before any layout
size query or Metal texture allocation. Preserve one-layer input
attachments (0020's 2D-array view), explicit linear row pitches (0019),
and seven-level optimal images, including imported host memory (0016).

Regression: host/moltenvk/repro/linear_images.c checks both image format
query entry points and binds deliberately invalid images if creation was
accepted. Before this patch all five invalid cases abort in Metal; four
valid controls pass, including an optimal host import viewed at mip six.
Run each case in a child process, following image_views.c, so one Metal
abort does not hide the remaining cases.

Generated-by: LLM
---
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
@@ -381,6 +381,8 @@
    default:
       UNREACHABLE("Invalid image type");
    }
+   /* Buffer-backed Metal textures cannot have mipmaps or array layers. These
+    * limits also apply to the LINEAR layout used for DRM modifier images. */
    if (pImageFormatInfo->tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR)
       maxArraySize = 1;
 
@@ -592,6 +594,23 @@
 {
    vk_image_init(&dev->vk, &image->vk, pCreateInfo);
 
+   /* Match the non-optimal limits advertised by the image format query before
+    * calculating a linear layout (which only allocates level 0). Metal aborts,
+    * rather than returning nil, on a buffer-backed mipmapped/array/3D/MSAA
+    * descriptor. Optimal host imports still use tiled textures and a private
+    * heap; importing memory must not impose these restrictions on them. */
+   if (image->vk.tiling != VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL &&
+       (image->vk.mip_levels != 1 || image->vk.array_layers != 1 ||
+        image->vk.image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D ||
+        image->vk.samples != VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT)) {
+      return vk_errorf(dev, VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED,
+                       "unsupported buffer-backed image: tiling %u, type %u, "
+                       "mips %u, layers %u, samples %u",
+                       image->vk.tiling, image->vk.image_type,
+                       image->vk.mip_levels, image->vk.array_layers,
+                       image->vk.samples);
+   }
+
    if ((image->vk.usage & (VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT |
                            VK_IMAGE_USAGE_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_BIT)) &&
        image->vk.samples > 1) {
